    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nLocated in the townland of Donoughboy, approximately 3km from the popular seaside resort of Kilkee in West Clare, this charming two-bedroom traditional stone-built cottage offers a blend of original character and modern comfort. Renovated, extended and modernised a number of years ago, the property extends to approximately 106.7 sq. mt. and retains many traditional features including sash-style windows, rough plaster finishes, high ceilings and exposed timber beams to mention a few. \n\nThe property also benefits from ample outdoor space, including a large pea gravel yard to the rear with a range of outbuildings and an adjoining paddock suitable for a variety of uses, which may also offer future development or site potential, subject to the necessary planning permission.\n\nThe property enjoys a peaceful countryside setting on a secondary road just off the Kilkee Cliff Walk route. Kilkee is renowned for its horseshoe-shaped beach and scenic cliff walks, with a full range of everyday amenities and services available in the town. The coastal villages of Carrigaholt and Doonbeg, together with the wider Loop Head Peninsula, are also within easy reach.\n\nCombining traditional cottage character with ample space in a countryside setting by the coast, viewing of this property is highly recommended and strictly by prior appointment with sole selling agents. PSL002295"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nFront Porch - 3m x 2.75m\nTile flooring, wrap around windows on three sides, rough plaster finish and double glass doors leading into main reception.\n\nMain Reception - 4.4m x 4.35m\nSolid timber flooring, front aspect window with timber shutters, high ceiling with exposed timber beams, raised solid fuel stove on raised liscannor flag, rough plaster finish to the walls, tv point, integrated exposed shelving, door to bedroom one, two and kitchen dining.\n\nBedroom One En-Suite - 4m x 3.7m\nSolid timber flooring, dual aspect windows to front and side with timber shutters, rough plaster finish to the walls, door to hotpress, access to attic storage and door to en-suite.\n\nEn-Suite - 3.6m x 2.45m\nTile flooring, rear aspect window, rough plaster finish to the walls, low level wc, wash hand basin with overhead wall mounted mirrored cabinet, corner fitted shower unit with pump shower and sliding glass panel doors and stand alone bath unit.\n\nBedroom Two En-Suite - 4.1m x 2.8m\nSolid timber flooring, dual aspect windows to the front and rear, high ceiling with timber beams, rough plaster finish to the walls and door to en-suite.\n\nEn-Suite - 2.45m x 2.1m\nTile flooring, front aspect window, rough plaster finish to the walls, low level wc, wash hand basin with overhead electric shaver point and light, corner fitted shower unit with electric shower, sliding glass panel doors and tile splash back.\n\nKitchen Dining Room - 7.2m x 3.4m\nTile flooring, two rear aspect windows and rear door access, recess ceiling lighting, decorative radiator cover, built-in wall and base units with ample work surfaces, tile splash back, integrated sink unit, extractor hood and fan, space and plumbing for electrical appliances including oven, fridge freezer, washing machine and dishwasher.\n\nOutbuildings - \nDivided into 4 units, stone built, approximately 20m x 4.05m.Storage shed, block built - 4.45m x 2.75m\n\nOutside - \nFront - Stone wall with plaster finish with pedestrian access to the front and vehicle access to the side, manicured lawns with mature plants and shrubs.Side - Paddock housing septic tank with own gated access.Rear - Pea gravel low maintenence yard, post and rail fencing to the side with block wall to the rear and an array of traditional outbuildings.\n\n"
      },
